# AgentPulse AI: environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development (`*.local` files are git-ignored).
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser, and they are baked
# into the public JavaScript bundle at build time, so never put secrets here.
#
# On Vercel, set these in Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables (for the
# Production and/or Preview environments), then redeploy: Vite reads them during
# the build, so an existing deployment will not pick up a change.

# Where the "Build your agent" blueprint form sends its leads.
# Any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST works, for example:
#   - a Formspree form:       https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxx
#   - a Zapier / Make / n8n webhook URL
#   - your own API route
# The browser posts directly to this URL, so the endpoint must allow cross-origin
# (CORS) requests from your site's domain.
#
# Payload: businessName, contactName, email, phone, monthlyVolume, industry,
# industryName, painPoints[], submittedAt (ISO 8601), page (URL of the page).
#
# Leave it empty and the form still works, but nothing is delivered: the browser
# console shows a warning and the confirmation screen makes no delivery promise.
VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT=
